---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="intro">
        Agora is a place to discuss the state of the world. People get so locked into one field that they lose
        their outlet to talk about what’s happening in the others. This is that outlet.
      </p>

      <h2>A Sunday</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>We start with the week’s news.</li>
        <li>Someone presents the reading everyone did beforehand and gives their take.</li>
        <li>We talk it out, over good food.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Readings take about ninety minutes and are always free. You leave up to date, knowing a little more about fields you don’t study, and knowing more people.</p>

      <h2>Ground rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Argue with ideas, not people.</li>
        <li>State the strongest version of a view before you criticize it.</li>
        <li>What’s said in a session stays there.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>No side taken</h2>
      <p>Agora takes no position on political, religious or ideological questions. It hosts the argument; it doesn’t settle it.</p>

      <p class="name">
        The name comes from the public square of ancient Athens, where citizens met to argue about the questions of
        the day.
      </p>

      <p><a href={url('/constitution')}>Read the constitution</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 36rem; }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 40px 0 12px; }
  ol, ul { margin: 0 0 1em; padding-left: 1.25em; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  li::marker { color: var(--stone); }
  .name { color: var(--stone); margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
